Z||000000||bHooper||06-11-2001||10:12 AM||||so, i've replaced the cracked cooling tube, and installed a new piece of hose from the water pump.<P>after burping the car (auto v-6), i have noticed that the anti freeze is slightly foamy!  what's up with that?<P>is there and anti foaming agent that i can use?  will this cause me problems?  i just need to run the car for one week (today is the absolute last day that i can work on it b4 the wedding on saturday).  unfortunatly, it is going to be in the high 80's and humid all week, so i will need the a/c.<P><BR>thanks!<BR><P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT 5 speed<BR>*Black '86 SE Automatic||||reg||4
Z||000001||FieroJoe||06-11-2001||10:55 AM||||Hmm, did you flush and totally refill the cooling system when you did all this?  That'd be the only suggestion I can offer.<P>Who knows what the previous owner put in there, I would just say get all the old crap out and start with fresh stuff and see if it does it again.<P>Also, air might be getting in the system because of another leak somewhere.  Check the new stuff you just replaced again and make sure you have everything connected air tight.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/joesig_1.jpg"> <BR>'87 Coupe 5spd.<BR>AIM:FieroJoe87||||reg||1
Z||000002||Jay||06-11-2001||12:21 PM||||What color is the foam?  If it is off white/brown that is oil in your cooling system and may be a cracked or warped head, or broken gasket.||||reg||1
Z||000003||bHooper||06-11-2001||12:37 PM||||no its white, or green white.  it just looks like "foamy" coolant.  <P>i did use a bit of 409 on the water pump, so that i could get the hose on.  perhaps some of that got into the coolant itself, and "foamed".<P>i just took it for a spin, seems to run ok.  i will check the coolant later this afternoon, b4 i leave for class.<P><P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT 5 speed<BR>*Black '86 SE Automatic||||reg||1
Z||000004||Jay||06-11-2001||12:57 PM||||Also check in your oil filler cap.  My 84 had a warped head and showed foam in the oil.||||reg||1
Z||000005||sqoach||06-11-2001||01:20 PM||||Sounds like it could be from the 409. Have you done a compression check? How does your oil look?||||reg||1
